    <!-- Help / Info Strings -->
    <string name="help_hub_title">Network Summary</string>
    <string name="help_hub_desc">This section shows your current active connection.\n\n• Signal Strength (dBm): The closer to zero, the stronger the signal (-60 excellent, -110 very weak).\n• Cell ID: Unique identifier of the cell tower you are connected to.</string>

    <string name="help_technical_title">Technical Details</string>
    <string name="help_technical_desc">• MCC/MNC: Country and operator codes.\n• eNb/CID: Base station and sector identity.\n• PCI/TAC: Physical identity and tracking area of the cell.\n• EARFCN/Band: Frequency and band information.\n• RSRP/RSRQ/SNR: Signal quality and noise ratios.</string>

    <string name="help_5g_title">5G NSA Details</string>
    <string name="help_5g_desc">5G NSA (Non-Standalone) is 5G technology using 4G infrastructure.\n\n• NR-ARFCN: 5G frequency channel.\n• SS-RSRP: 5G signal strength.\n• SS-SINR: 5G signal purity (higher is better).</string>

    <string name="help_wifi_title">Wi-Fi Details</string>
    <string name="help_wifi_desc">• RSSI: Wi-Fi signal strength.\n• Link Speed: Theoretical speed between device and router.\n• Channel/Frequency: The band Wi-Fi is broadcasting on (2.4GHz or 5GHz).\n• DNS/Gateway: Network routing information.</string>

    <string name="help_performance_title">Performance Test</string>
    <string name="help_performance_desc">• Ping: Data round-trip time (lower is better).\n• Download: Speed of downloading data from internet.\n• Upload: Speed of uploading data to internet.\n\nNote: The test takes 10 seconds and calculates the real average.</string>
</resources>
